"""
Electronic power switch (MOSFET or IGBT) as a resistance that the gate command moves between an
on and an off value, with the device's output capacitance across it. The standard library has
no switch, so the channel is its `VariableResistor`.

    R = R_off (R_on / R_off)^g        v = R i_channel        i = i_channel + C_oss dv/dt

`g` is the gate command: 0 holds the switch off at `R_off`, 1 holds it on at `R_on`, and the
values between are the turn-on and turn-off transitions, which a `PWM` block ramps over a finite
time. The interpolation is geometric: an equal step in `g` multiplies `R` by an equal factor, so
during a ramp the resistance sweeps the whole range at an even pace. That is what makes current
and voltage overlap while the switch changes state, and the overlap is the switching loss. A
switch that jumped from off to on would dissipate nothing while switching.

Hard-switching an inductive current `I` against a voltage `V` with a linear ramp of `g` over
`t_sw` dissipates `2 V I t_sw / ln(R_off / R_on)` per edge (derived: the current, or the voltage,
follows `R` exponentially for the part of the ramp where the other is clamped). With the
defaults that is `0.109 V I t_sw`, the textbook `V I t / 2` of an edge `0.22 t_sw` long. While
fully on the switch burns `R_on i^2`, the deck's `R_DSon I^2` conduction loss. The channel
conducts both ways, like a MOSFET's; a freewheeling diode is a separate part.

The output capacitance `C_oss` is what a real switch node slews through, and the model needs it
for the same reason: without it the node between a switch and a diode has no state, and at each
turn-on the solver has to jump the node from the diode's drop to the supply in one algebraic
step. At 1e-6 tolerances that jump fails on the second pulse of the buck chopper. With `C_oss`
the node voltage is continuous, and the capacitor adds only its `C_oss V^2 / 2` per turn-on to
the loss (0.02 W in the buck at 48 V and 20 kHz).

Defaults are a low-voltage power MOSFET (assumed). `P_loss` is the power the channel
dissipates, conduction and switching together; the capacitor stores energy and dissipates none.
"""
component Switch
  extends ElectricalComponents.Analog.Interfaces.TwoPin
  "Gate command: 0 off, 1 on, between is a transition"
  g = RealInput() {^g}
  channel = ElectricalComponents.Analog.Basic.VariableResistor() {^channel}
  "Holds the channel's heat port; the resistance has no temperature coefficient"
  ambient = ThermalComponents.Sources.FixedTemperature(T = 300.15) {^ambient}
  capacitance = ElectricalComponents.Analog.Basic.Capacitor(C = C_oss) {^capacitance}
  "Resistance when on, R_DSon (assumed)"
  parameter R_on::Resistance = 10.0e-3
  "Resistance when off; leakage v / R_off (assumed)"
  parameter R_off::Resistance = 1.0e6
  "Output capacitance across the switch (assumed)"
  parameter C_oss::Capacitance = 1.0e-9
  "Current into p, through the switch and its capacitance, out of n"
  variable i::Current
  "Current through the channel alone"
  variable i_channel::Current
  "Resistance set by the gate"
  variable R::Resistance
  "Power dissipated in the channel"
  variable P_loss::Power
relations
  connect(p, channel.p, capacitance.p) {^id1}
  connect(channel.n, capacitance.n, n) {^id2}
  connect(channel.heat_port, ambient.port) {^id3}
  R = R_off * (R_on / R_off) ^ g
  channel.R = R
  i = p.i
  i_channel = channel.i
  P_loss = channel.LossPower
metadata {
  "Dyad": {"icons": {"default": "dyad://VehicleSystemsComponents/Vehicle/Electric/Switch.svg"}, "labels": [{"label": "$(instance)", "x": 500, "y": 1000, "rot": 0}]},
  "_links": {
    "p": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"iconName": "pos", "x1": -50, "y1": 450, "x2": 50, "y2": 550}, "diagram": {"iconName": "pos", "x1": -50, "y1": 450, "x2": 50, "y2": 550}}}},
    "n": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"iconName": "neg", "x1": 950, "y1": 450, "x2": 1050, "y2": 550}, "diagram": {"iconName": "neg", "x1": 950, "y1": 450, "x2": 1050, "y2": 550}}}},
    "g": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 450, "y1": -50, "x2": 550, "y2": 50, "rot": 90}, "diagram": {"x1": 450, "y1": -50, "x2": 550, "y2": 50, "rot": 90}}}},
    "channel": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 400, "y1": 300, "x2": 600, "y2": 500}}}},
    "capacitance": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 400, "y1": 600, "x2": 600, "y2": 800}}}},
    "ambient": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 700, "y1": 100, "x2": 900, "y2": 300, "rot": 180}}}}
  }
}
end
